tcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01PSsJ8EWsXusfX5h5xU1YDC", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53233, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01PSsJ8EWsXusfX5h5xU1YDC", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 54825, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_013rSLY5GZujZ69eB4eKGAjn", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55125, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_013rSLY5GZujZ69eB4eKGAjn", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55125, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013rSLY5GZujZ69eB4eKGAjn", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 59119, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions and healthy again. The error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%. SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open, which pages on-call.\n\n1. **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy. v2.3.1 and its release candidate v2.3.1-rc were both unhealthy. My first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I retried once and it completed in all regions.\n2. **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback (including the stop partway through), the current state and two follow-ups:\n   - Find out why v2.3.1 is failing.\n   - Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the rollback.\n\n   The request to create the incident timed out, but the incident list showed it had been created, so I didn't send it again. That avoided opening a duplicate and paging on-call twice.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Mv7LNSsMCn5s4R5Y2g7yRe", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01YVsr3qowcLdvQRVFk2BPgR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01SaL3uxqmzhq3r3pUmuQnQw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Gg4tLMj6iQe5LPYRsg5KsM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version again should be safe to repeat, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01JtfscFKnL5Suk7Rr9h6zPi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01EWD5QSkPbRKnLyuYf3LMN3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01F5eKLu1frPTL57SLQ2VtTk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PSsJ8EWsXusfX5h5xU1YDC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failed health checks after the latest deploy, with an error rate of about 18% in us-east, us-west and eu-west. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving the regions on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). A retry finished the rollback. All regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_013rSLY5GZujZ69eB4eKGAjn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions and healthy again. The error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%. SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open, which pages on-call.\n\n1. **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy. v2.3.1 and its release candidate v2.3.1-rc were both unhealthy. My first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I retried once and it completed in all regions.\n2. **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback (including the stop partway through), the current state and two follow-ups:\n   - Find out why v2.3.1 is failing.\n   - Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the rollback.\n\n   The request to create the incident timed out, but the incident list showed it had been created, so I didn't send it again. That avoided opening a duplicate and paging on-call twice.", "type": "text"}]}]}